title: Genesis 14 – Melchizedek
description: A study in Genesis 14: Abram rescues Lot, refuses the spoils of Sodom, and gives tithes to Melchizedek, king of Salem and priest of the most high God.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-14-melchizedek.html

=== Introduction
--- Melchizedek [title]
overline: A study in Genesis 14
sub: King of Salem, priest of the most high God.
refs: Genesis 14:18-20; Hebrews 7:1-3
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== The war of the kings
--- They took Lot
scripture: Genesis 14:11-12 | mark: they took Lot, Abram’s brother’s son, who dwelt in Sodom
p: Lot, who we saw pitch his tent toward Sodom, now dwelt in Sodom, and was punished, spoiled and taken into captivity by the other kings’ armies. [[Genesis 13:12]]

--- Abram armed his servants
scripture: Genesis 14:13-16 | mark: he armed his trained servants
p: Abram, seeing his brother in faith, his nephew Lot, taken, seeks his rescue. He is not part of the war of the kings itself. But he is the finisher of it, with God’s hand defeating his foes and freeing Lot and his people and possessions.

=== King of Salem
--- Bread and wine
scripture: Genesis 14:18-20 | mark: brought forth bread and wine: and he was the priest of the most high God; he gave him tithes of all
p: Melchizedek, king of peace, priest of the {Lord} God, Jehovah. God the Father.
big: Psalm 110:4

--- Made like unto the Son of God
scripture: Hebrews 7:1-3 | mark: King of righteousness; King of peace; made like unto the Son of God; abideth a priest continually
p: As always, the New Testament is the best study guide for the Old Testament. Here Paul gives us understanding of who exactly Melchizedek, king of Salem, priest of the most high God, was, or at least pictures: Jesus Christ.

--- The less is blessed of the better
scripture: Hebrews 7:4-10 | mark: without all contradiction the less is blessed of the better; Levi also, who receiveth tithes, payed tithes in Abraham
p: Paul uses him as an example of a non-Levitical priest to whom tithes and honour are due: a pattern of Jesus, and of the priesthood of believers in Christ Himself. The less was blessed by the greater: *Blessed be Abram of the most high God, possessor of heaven and earth*. [[Genesis 14:19-20]] [[1 Peter 2:9]]

--- After the order of Melchisedec
scripture: Hebrews 7:11-17 | mark: after the power of an endless life
refs: Hebrews 7:18-22

--- Able to save to the uttermost
scripture: Hebrews 7:24-27 | mark: he is able also to save them to the uttermost
refs: Hebrews 7:28

=== Christ in the Old Testament
--- A theophany
lead: The appearance of Jesus throughout the Old Testament, when the {Lord} speaks in person to the patriarchs, is called a “theophany.”
tile: Genesis 22 | Stays Abraham’s hand over Isaac [[Genesis 22:11-12]]
tile: Genesis 32 | Wrestles with Jacob [[Genesis 32:24-30]]
tile: Daniel 3 | In the fiery furnace [[Daniel 3:25]]
p: Most believers see Jesus in the angel of the {Lord} passages: the {Lord} who meets with and speaks to the patriarchs. As the Bible is one story, telling us about God, Jesus, the Holy Ghost and the Godhead’s relationship with man, Jesus appears in every book of the Old Testament, regardless of manifestation. [[Luke 24:27]]

--- It was always about Jesus
lead: Here Melchizedek is seen as an early appearance of Jesus: taking tithes from Abraham, the king of peace, the priest of the high God. Without beginning or end, no mother or father given, *made like unto the Son of God; abideth a priest continually*.
callout: I believe it is Jesus, personally. But either way, it’s a sign that the ordinance of bread and wine, of faith in God as Saviour, as the faith of the patriarchs, was always about Jesus. [[Matthew 26:26-29]]

=== The spoils of Sodom
--- Not a thread nor a shoelatchet
scripture: Genesis 14:21-24 | mark: I will not take from a thread even to a shoelatchet
p: Abram refuses spoils from the king of Sodom, not wanting anything from that wicked man. He did what he did because it was right. He rejects the treasure, but a tenth of the spoils was given to Melchizedek as an offering to God. Because all things are God’s. [[Psalm 24:1]]

--- What believers look like
lead: This should be a picture of what the action of saved believers looks like.
panel: Stay out of the war | Not getting entangled in commitments with the wicked. [[2 Timothy 2:4]]
panel: Seek no treasure | Not a thread nor a shoelatchet from Sodom.
panel: Defend the brethren | Defending brethren from violence, and having faith in God to destroy our enemies when we do defend the righteous.

=== Close
--- A priest for ever [title]
overline: Genesis 14
point: Abram delivered Lot | Not part of the war, but the finisher of it, by God’s hand.
point: Melchizedek | King of righteousness, King of peace, made like unto the Son of God.
point: Christ our High Priest | A priest for ever after the order of Melchisedec, able to save to the uttermost.
point: Nothing from Sodom | All things are God’s.

